[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[m\u001b[H\u001b[JWindows PowerShell\r\nCopyright (C) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.\u001b[4;1HPS D:\\Developer\\EcoIq>  \u001b[92m$env:CODETERM_SESSION_BINDING_NONCE\u001b[90m=\u001b[36m'13e17546-8830-444c-92ea-01b11ebd5a84'\u001b[37m;\u001b[m \u001b[93mcodex\u001b[m \u001b[37mresume\u001b[m \u001b[90m--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\u001b[m \u001b[36m'019fb172-bfaa-7bf1-bd4b-1f4bd4db8485'\r\n\u001b[39;2m\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\r\n\u2502 >_ \u001b[1mOpenAI Codex\u001b[2m (v0.146.0)                  \u2502\r\n\u2502                                             \u2502\r\n\u2502 model:       \u001b[mgpt-5.5 low\u001b[2m   \u001b[36;22m/model\u001b[39;2m to change \u2502\r\n\u2502 directory:   \u001b[mD:\\Developer\\EcoIq\u001b[2m             \u2502\r\n\u2502 permissions: \u001b[35;1mYOLO mode\u001b[39;2m                      \u2502\r\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\u001b[13;1H\u001b[m  \u001b[1mTip:\u001b[m Try the \u001b[1mDesktop app\u001b[m. Run 'codex app' or visit https://chatgpt.com/codex?app-landing-page=true\u001b[15;1H\u001b[48;2;41;41;41m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[2m\u203a \u001b[22mRead the CodeTerm role, team, counterpart, and coordination instructions provided by the host. Acknowledge your role and counterpart, then wait for a user goal or orchestration request.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[49;2m\u2022 \u001b[mAcknowledged. I\u2019m the CodeTerm Planner for workspace \u001b[36mEcoIq\u001b[m, Team \u001b[36mnot yet established\u001b[m, with no bound plan yet.\u001b[21;1H  My Orchestrator counterpart is Planck in tab \u001b[36m56897936\u001b[m; I\u2019ll coordinate through that tab and won\u2019t spawn duplicates or create planning structure until there\u2019s a user goal or explicit orchestration request.\u001b[23;1H  Ready and waiting.\u001b[25;1H\u001b[2m\u2022 \u001b[mYou have 1 usage limit reset available. Run /usage to use one.\u001b[27;1H\u001b[48;2;41;41;41m \u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1mSelect Model and Effort\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[2mAccess legacy models by running codex -m <model_name> or in your config.toml\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n \u001b[K\r\n  1. gpt-5.6-sol (default)  \u001b[2mLatest frontier agentic coding model.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n  2. gpt-5.6-terra          \u001b[2mBalanced agentic coding model for everyday work.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n  3. gpt-5.6-luna           \u001b[2mFast and affordable agentic coding model.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[36;1m\u203a 4. gpt-5.5 (current)      Frontier model for complex coding, research, and real-world work.\u001b[39;22m\u001b[K\r\n  5. gpt-5.4                \u001b[2mStrong model for everyday coding.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n  6. gpt-5.4-mini           \u001b[2mSmall, fast, and cost-efficient model for simpler coding tasks.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n  7. gpt-5.3-codex-spark    \u001b[2mUltra-fast coding model.\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\n \u001b[K\u001b[39;3H\u001b[49;2mPress enter to confirm or esc to go back                                                                                                                                                                                                      \u001b[m\u001b[?25l\u001b[39;240H\u001b[2m \u001b[m"]
